{"v":1,"kind":"chunk","id":"","file":"internal/web/handlers.go","side":"new","start":81,"end":81,"title":"A new revision redraws the page, not only the panel","surface":"internal/web/handlers.go","before":"the stream only ever pushed the panel, so a revision left a stale diff on screen until someone reloaded","after":"the head sha moving sends the page fragment, the panel one otherwise","decision":"one fragment per thing that can change, picked by what actually moved, so the smallest correct piece travels","rejected":"telling the browser to reload itself, which throws away the selection and scroll position","author":"","at":""}
{"v":1,"kind":"chunk","id":"","file":"internal/web/templates/page.html","side":"new","start":9,"end":9,"title":"The delta of one revision, on its own page","surface":"?since=N","before":"coming back to a proposal meant rereading all of it to find what the last revision changed","after":"since=N diffs from that revision instead of the base, with a toggle in the header","decision":"the base of the diff is a parameter, so one page answers both questions and there is nothing to keep in step","rejected":"a separate revisions page, which would drift from this one the first time either changed","author":"","at":""}
{"v":1,"kind":"chunk","id":"","file":"internal/web/templates/page.html","side":"new","start":32,"end":32,"title":"A decision says was, now and call","surface":"the decisions block","before":"a struck-through phrase, an arrow, and a line that started with not:","after":"four labelled rows: was, now, call, and instead of","decision":"label every field, because a reader should not have to decode a layout to read a sentence","rejected":"keeping the arrow and explaining it in a legend nobody reads twice","author":"","at":""}
{"v":1,"kind":"chunk","id":"","file":"internal/patch/patch.go","side":"new","start":70,"end":70,"title":"The header counts what the diff did","surface":"internal/patch","before":"the page opened on a wall of lines with no idea of how big the change was","after":"the proposal and each file carry their added and removed counts","decision":"count in the parser, where the lines already are, so nothing reads the diff a second time","rejected":"asking git for numstat, which is another process and another format to parse","author":"","at":""}
{"v":1,"kind":"chunk","id":"","file":"internal/review/handover.go","side":"new","start":14,"end":14,"title":"The whole review, handed over once","surface":"githerb handover","before":"notes were relayed to the agent one at a time, which is the slow half of reviewing","after":"one button copies every open note, where it points, and the command that answers it","decision":"the brief is domain text, so the button and the command hand over the same words","rejected":"a webhook that poked an agent nobody has configured yet","author":"","at":""}
